<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Notification small icon for the SOS lifeline and gentle reminders.

  WHY THIS EXISTS
  Both SosNotificationService and GentleReminderService passed
  '@mipmap/ic_launcher' to AndroidInitializationSettings. flutter_local_notifications
  resolves that with

      context.getResources().getIdentifier(name, "drawable", packageName)

  so it searches the DRAWABLE folder for a resource literally NAMED
  "@mipmap/ic_launcher". That lookup returns 0 in every build, debug included,
  and the plugin throws invalid_icon. The boot-time catch swallowed it into a log
  line ("[boot] sos init skipped"), so the SOS lifeline had never initialised
  and nothing anywhere reported it. A safety feature was dead and silent.

  Even a corrected mipmap reference would still be wrong twice over:
    1. the plugin looks in drawable, not mipmap;
    2. res/mipmap-*/ic_launcher.png is ORPHANED, because AndroidManifest declares
       android:icon="@mipmap/launcher_icon". Resource shrinking therefore
       DELETES ic_launcher from release builds. Verified absent from the
       release APK.

  Android 8.0+ renders the small icon as a mask tinted to the system colour, so
  this must be a solid white silhouette on transparent. The colourful adaptive
  launcher icon is the wrong asset here regardless of the lookup.

  NOTE: an XML comment may not contain a double hyphen. An earlier revision of
  this comment used them for parenthetical asides and failed the build at
  parseReleaseLocalResources with a fatal error about an illegal string in a
  comment. Do not add one here.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24">
    <!-- Shield: the "safety plan / lifeline" read, and legible at status-bar size. -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF"
        android:pathData="M12,2L4,4.9v6.4c0,4.9 3.4,9.4 8,10.7c4.6,-1.3 8,-5.8 8,-10.7V4.9L12,2z" />
</vector>